Replaces the 200KB+ picomatch dependency with ~30 lines of custom glob pattern matching code.

## Implementation

- **Pattern normalization**: Convert both patterns and paths to forward slashes, eliminating platform-specific escaping complexity
- **Regex conversion**: Map glob patterns (`*`, `**`, `**/path/**`) to equivalent regular expressions
- **Matcher function**: Test normalized absolute paths against compiled patterns

## Supported Patterns

- `*` - matches within path segment
- `**` - matches across segments  
- `**/path/**` - matches directory and contents
- Case-insensitive matching via `insensitive` option

## Code

```typescript
function globToRegex(pattern: string, insensitive: boolean): RegExp {
  pattern = pattern.replace(/\\/g, "/");
  const endsWithDoubleStar = pattern.endsWith("/**");

  let regex = pattern
    .replace(/[.+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&")
    .replace(/\*\*/g, "__DOUBLESTAR__")
    .replace(/\*/g, "[^/]*")
    .replace(/__DOUBLESTAR__/g, ".*");

  if (endsWithDoubleStar) {
    regex = `^${regex.slice(0, -3)}(?:/.*)?$`;
  } else {
    regex = `^${regex}$`;
  }

  return new RegExp(regex, insensitive ? "i" : "");
}
```

The normalized path approach handles Windows backslashes without special cases, keeping the implementation simple and maintainable.

