HTTP 400 and 429 errors prevented database operations on `/_spark/kv/` endpoints. All requests from nginx appeared as originating from the proxy IP (172.18.0.1), causing shared rate limit bucket exhaustion. Application makes 12+ concurrent requests on page load.

## Changes

- **Trust proxy headers**: Added `app.set('trust proxy', 1)` to read real client IPs from `X-Forwarded-For`
- **Rate limit adjustment**: Increased from 100 to 500 requests per 15 minutes (~6.7 → ~33 req/min)
- **Middleware ordering**: Moved rate limiter after body parser

```typescript
// Before: rate limiter applied first, sees all requests from 172.18.0.1
app.use('/api/', limiter);
app.use(bodyParser.json());

// After: proper client IP detection, per-user rate limiting
app.set('trust proxy', 1);
app.use(bodyParser.json());
app.use('/api/', limiter);
```

Requests are now rate-limited per actual client IP rather than globally at the proxy level.

