### Motivation

This implementation adds support for per-issuer OIDC configuration while maintaining full backward compatibility.

Configuration format:
```json
{
  "issuers": {
    "https://issuer1.com": {
      "allowedAudiences": "aud1,aud2",
      "userNameClaim": "sub",
      "staticKeyFile": "/path/to/key.pem"
    },
    "https://issuer2.com": {
      "allowedAudiences": "aud3",
      "userNameClaim": "email"
    }
  }
}
```

User asked if the app sends data to Google Sheets and requested 100% offline functionality matching frc2713.github.io/QRScout/.

## Changes

**Offline-first architecture**
- Removed blocking Google Sign-In script from HTML `<head>` that prevented offline operation
- Dynamic script loading with 5s timeout fallback
- Race condition prevention via `scriptLoadCompleted` flag ensuring single callback execution
- Applied timeout protection to both initial load and retry flows

```javascript
function loadGoogleLibrary() {
    let scriptLoadCompleted = false;

    const timeout = setTimeout(() => {
        if (!scriptLoadCompleted && !googleLibraryLoaded) {
            scriptLoadCompleted = true;
            onGoogleLibraryError();
        }
    }, 5000);

    const script = document.createElement('script');
    script.onload = () => {
        if (!scriptLoadCompleted) {
            scriptLoadCompleted = true;
            clearTimeout(timeout);
            onGoogleLibraryLoad();
        }
    };
    // ...
}
```

**Simplified sending logic**
- Removed IndexedDB queue cleanup (unused)
- Added upfront `navigator.onLine` check with explicit "no auto-retry" messaging
- Enhanced error messaging for connection loss during send

**Documentation**
- Added HOW_IT_WORKS.md confirming both sending methods work (Apps Script, Sheets API)
- Updated README.md with "YES, it sends data" header
- Service worker cache v4→v5

## Result

App loads and operates 100% offline once cached. Data sending requires internet (checked upfront, clear user feedback). Google Sign-In loads non-blocking when available.

